            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KATYPI"
            },
            "reviewBody": "One Friday evening after a particularly trying work week, I made this. I altered the recipe slightly; I added a whipped cream and a couple of swipes of nutmeg across my grater. The effect was multidimensional. The mug was warm in my hands, the heady aroma of nutmeg assailed my nose, the cloud of whipped cream was silky on my lips, and then the velvety taste of the coffee and Baileys slid across my pallet. An immediate AHHHH reponse came over me, and all was right with the world once again. Love this!"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chef V"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Nothing to not love about coffee and Irish cream. \nI used Bailey's. Also added a teaspoon of espresso powder to my coffee as I enjoy the combination. \nA nice treat on a weekend or whenever you need something special.",
            "datePublished": "2016-03-09T08:12:54.807Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Bossier"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used to make this for my after dinner dessert for my dates. I would light the Irish cream and pour the hot coffee into the burning cream, then added whipped cream. Very impressive--and great tasting!!",
            "datePublished": "2010-06-28T02:07:55.810Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Tammy Lynn"
            },
            "reviewBody": "My mother-in-law really got me into this drink. They always have Irish cream (heck, she's from Ireland). She likes to add a little half and half and some brown sugar to hers. However, I think it's perfect just like this. I try to keep this on hand in the fall/winter from now on.",
            "datePublished": "2016-05-06T20:25:24.797Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "sewjean"
            },
            "reviewBody": "For those of you who like the flavor, but don't want the alcohol. Use an Irish Cream flavoring by Torani. It doesn't have the cream, but a dab of whipped cream will help. The flavor is wonderful. The flavorings can be found at most bar supply or wholesale markets. Very reasonable also. A little goes a long long way.",
            "datePublished": "2012-03-07T10:00:04.153Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BJDURHAM"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is my beverage of choice on a cold evening when I can't get my feet warm. I add half &amp; half (in the same amount that I usually add to my morning coffee) along with the Irish cream for a smooth, warming cuppa.",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-06T10:00:42.523Z"
